    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Processes are BPMN, and the diagrams are executable",
      "prov:value": "**Do not quote a count of diagrams from prose.** This repository's own\n`AGENTS.md` said \"six `.bpmn` files\" long after there were far more, in a file\nthat elsewhere warns against exactly that. Count the directory."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "There is no `tool` element, and that is a decision",
      "prov:value": "It would also put the edge on the wrong side. `satisfies` is owned by the Tool,\nwhich knows what it implements and is versioned with it; a `tool` ref would be\nowned by the diagram author, who would have to track Tools across every\ninstance — measured 2026-09-26, **116** Tools are discovered from four\n`tools/` graphs (`cat-harness`, the DAK layer, the content core,\nthe FHIR IG layer), so a diagram in one instance would be asserting facts about\nthree others.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-26"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-26"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "There is no `tool` element, and that is a decision",
      "prov:value": "**What is NOT being claimed** is that the join is well populated. Measured the\nsame day over the authoritative registry (`tools/discover.ts`, never a grep):"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A Tool's OWN procedure is the Tool's subprocess, not the skill's prose",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-30 (placement ruling 6): *\"in general tools can describe\ntheir own specific subprocesses if needed to not bog down general skills\"*.\nThe direction of the edge stays the one above — the Tool owns it. A Tool\nwhose way of exercising a skill has steps of its own (a retry loop, a staging\ndirectory, a two-pass mode) names that diagram in **`subprocesses`**, a list\nof process ids on its Tool node; `check:tools` refuses one no `.bpmn` in the\ncheckout has as its stem. The general process stays general and reaches the\ndetail by `calledElement` only where it has chosen that Tool. By convention\nthe diagram sits in the declaring instance's `processes/tools/` concern\ngroup, beside other tools' procedures rather than among the general\nprocesses.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A process binds only skills its instance can reach (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-03: a process may bind only skills (and, through them, Tools)\nfrom **its own instance or one it `needs`**, transitively, *\"general rule, not\njust fhir-harness\"*. A `<bootstrap.processes:skill ref>` to a skill that only\na HIGHER instance holds is a wrong-direction edge, the same as an upward\nimport: the diagram cannot be lifted into its own repository without the layer\nabove it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A process binds only skills its instance can reach (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "`bun run cat check:process-bindings` gates it, with the same `allowedFromNeeds`\ndirection as `check:import-direction` and `check:reference-direction`.\n**`skill-ref-resolves` does not catch this, and that is why the gate exists:**\nit resolves against `knownSkills(root)`, which in a pre-split checkout is\ncheckout-scoped, so \"resolves\" means \"exists somewhere\". On 2026-10-03 that\nhid 33 wrong-direction bindings in 9 diagrams behind a green audit. They are\nin a ratchet baseline, cleared under bean `mlux`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mlux",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A process binds only skills its instance can reach (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "**The two say so about each other** (owner, 2026-10-04, option 1 of 3):\n`skill-ref-resolves` is existence only, and its own summary names this gate\nas the answer on direction. That leaves one implementation of \"may this process\nbind this skill\", not two free to disagree.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Binding the extension namespaces",
      "prov:value": "**An element's prefix names the Subgraph that declares it** (owner, 2026-09-24,\nbean `12s9`). A diagram binds one address per vocabulary it uses:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 12s9",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Binding the extension namespaces",
      "prov:value": "Readers match **the address, never the prefix text**, so a diagram that binds a\ndifferent prefix to the same address reads identically, and `folio:` bound to\nanyone else's address is not ours. The older single address,\n`…/folio-assistant/bpmn`, is **retired** (2026-09-24). An element under it is\nno longer read, and `external-schemas` reports a diagram that still binds it\nas drift. A test fails if an element is written under an address whose\nvocabulary does not define it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Edge routing: rectilinear, and never over a task",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-23, on `document-ingestion`'s rendered diagram: **\"keep\nrectilinear if possible, no overlapping.\"** Two rules, and the second is the\none that actually bites.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Edge routing: rectilinear, and never over a task",
      "prov:value": "**Never over a task, a lane label or another edge.** The case that prompted\nthis: the `gap` flow from *Record the gap as a bean* back to *Derive content\nfrom the assets* was drawn as one long diagonal crossing the full width of the\nprocess, passing under every task in the lane. It is a perfectly ordinary\nloop-back and it was the hardest edge on the page to follow."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Edge routing: rectilinear, and never over a task",
      "prov:value": "**Check it by looking at the rendered SVG, not the XML.** Waypoints that look\norderly in source can still emit a diagonal, and `render:bpmn` is what a reader\nsees. The rendered page is the artefact under review — `preview:site` exists\nfor exactly this reason, after a generator shipped 22 headings with one anchor\nand every gate was green across it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Rendering: what a reader can click, and what must not collide",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-11-03 (cat-harness#991), on the published diagrams: *\"linked\ntasks should be on the task title only, not the whole box. the subprocess\nshould be opened by the [+] not the whole box.\"* `render:bpmn`\n(`cat-harness-tools/src/workflow/diagram-links.ts`) draws the links; the\nlayout rules are checked by `bpmn:detangle`\n([`bpmn-detangle`](bpmn-detangle.md)).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "cat-harness#991",
        "2026-11-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A bean-marked step performs the operation, not a note about it",
      "prov:value": "**You do not draw `claim`, `resolve` or `archive` yourself.** They live in two\ncalled processes and nowhere else (bean `folio-assistant-m8gz`, owner\n2026-10-24): `Process_BeanOpen` (`sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn`: check,\ncreate, whose bean, claim or leave alone) and `Process_BeanClose`\n(`sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn`: complete or scrap, then one shared archive\nstep; or record the blocker and hand back). A process that works on a bean\ncalls OPEN where the bean becomes its own, follows it with a `claimed` /\n`not yours` gateway, and calls CLOSE straight before each end it reaches from\nthere. `note` stays on the steps where the work happens. `check:bean-calls`\n(run inside `check:workflow-refs`) refuses the three ops anywhere else, and a\nprocess that calls one of the pair without the other. Why: 219 beans resolved\nand never archived, and 7 processes that claimed and never closed —\n[`todo-manager`](../../../work-plan/skills/work-plan/todo-manager.md) §\"Archiving — two dispositions\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean m8gz",
        "2026-10-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-24"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
